Status of this copy: UNMODIFIED, PARTIAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  This is unmodified third-party material vendored for reference only. No file
  taken from upstream has been edited, reformatted, or re-encoded; each is a
  byte-for-byte copy of the file at the commit named above. This was verified
  mechanically: all 1536 vendored files were compared against the upstream
  clone and all 1536 matched exactly, and every vendored path was confirmed to
  be an upstream git-tracked path.

  This copy is a SUBSET, not the whole repository. The full upstream tree is
  2491 tracked paths and 352 MB checked out, which is too large to commit here.
  The subset rule applied — reproducible from a fresh clone at the pinned
  commit — was:

    1. drop `doc/content/media/`      (711 files; figures, screenshots, video)
    2. drop any file >= 1 MiB          (32 files; binary meshes, multigroup
                                        cross-section libraries, large data)
    3. drop Git LFS pointer stubs      (73 files; upstream stores these assets
                                        in LFS, so a plain clone yields only
                                        132-byte pointers, not the content)
    4. drop `.git/`, `.github/`, `.civet/`, `.gitattributes`, `.gitmodules`,
       and upstream's own `.gitignore`  (see the note below — dropping it is
                                        load-bearing, not cosmetic)
    5. drop `apps/`                    (empty submodule mount points; the
                                        submodules resolve to INL-internal
                                        hosts such as github.inl.gov and are
                                        not publicly cloneable)

  Note on the dropped Git control files. Upstream's `.gitignore` is a MOOSE
  build-artifact ignore list that ignores `*.csv`, `*.xml`, `*.txt`, `*.e`,
  `*.dat` and `*.png` wholesale; upstream keeps those files in tree only because
  they were force-added before the rules applied. Carried into this repository it
  would have silently dropped 57 genuine reference files (material property CSVs,
  OpenMC geometry/materials XML, orifice-coordinate tables) from the commit.
  Likewise `.gitattributes` declares `filter=lfs` on paths whose content is not
  LFS-backed in this copy. Both are build plumbing for a repository that is
  compiled and run; nothing here is compiled or run, so both were removed. No
  content file was altered.

  What was kept: every MOOSE/Griffin/Pronghorn/BISON/SAM/Nek/Cardinal/OpenMC
  input deck, every documentation markdown page, and the gold/reference result
  CSVs. That is the reference value of the VTB for this project. See
  `INVENTORY.md` for the contents and for the list of excluded large files.

  Nothing here is compiled, linked, or executed by any crate in this workspace.
  None of it is packaged into a published crate: it lives outside `crates/`, and
  Cargo only packages files beneath a crate's own directory.

  To obtain an excluded asset, clone upstream at the pinned commit and fetch
  Git LFS content:

      git clone https://github.com/idaholab/virtual_test_bed
      cd virtual_test_bed
      git checkout f3314028132912e5b02b9040d9e7cc60290fce4b
      git lfs pull

